+# Orchestra management evidence
+
+The project stays on its current Cloudflare Workers/D1 stack. Orchestra manages the technical lifecycle; the operator dashboard retains preschool business operations.
+
+- `/api/health`: existing liveness/configuration contract, unchanged. It does not call a model or test D1.
+- `/api/ready`: bounded, read-only `SELECT 1` against D1; returns 200 only on success, otherwise 503. It does not seed data or call Gemini/n8n.
+- `/api/version`: `{ "sha": "<40-character commit>" }` when `BUILD_SHA` is set; otherwise null.
+- Both frontend builds emit `/version.json`. Clean builds derive their Git commit. Dirty local builds emit null unless BUILD_SHA is explicitly supplied.
+
+For a reviewed API deployment, supply `BUILD_SHA` for the actual commit through the existing deployment process. Example: `npm run deploy -- --var BUILD_SHA:<full-commit>`. This documentation does not authorize a deployment. Deployments remain manual and under the hosting owner's control. Do not apply remote migrations as part of local checks.
+
+`npm run test:d1` runs migrations and the readiness query against an isolated local D1 database and removes its scratch state. It explicitly uses `--local` and passes no cloud/model credentials. Wrangler is pinned in engine development dependencies. GitHub Actions runs unit/type/build/local-D1 checks; it does not deploy or call a model. Existing live eval commands can make model calls and are excluded.
+
+Before real family data is accepted, add authentication/authorization to administrative and sensitive-read interfaces, prevent unauthenticated resets, and protect model-backed public interfaces against abuse. The current prototype deliberately has no authentication. Orchestra's login does not protect this app. This patch does not claim to fix that blocker.
